# An object with two implementations of one method, in the mixin encoding
# of inheritance (corpora/contest_mixin_library.pl): problems of the
# reduction series whose answer is a finite set of binary naturals, asked
# whole, as the set of their normal forms.
#
# THE CLASS has three slots, run, step and start, and is the set
# {Base, Increment_1, ..., Increment_m}, Base = {Run, Start}:
# - Run is the template method, run n accumulator = n accumulator
#   (\p. run p (step accumulator)), which applies step n times to the
#   accumulator without knowing where step comes from;
# - Start is start = 0;
# - Increment_i is step x = x + a_i, with the binary plus of
#   contest_merge_dynamic.pl.
# The object is {Base, Increment_1, ..., Increment_m}, and the program
# reads run n start. Two mixins implement step, so step is their
# union, and each call of step chooses again: two implementations of one
# slot give two sets of answers, which is the intended meaning. The answers are the
# sums of n increments, n a_1 .. n a_m: for the increments {1, 2}, the
# n + 1 values n .. 2n, reached along 2^n paths.
#
# WHAT IT ASKS. The accumulator after k steps is spelled by the choices
# that built it, (0 + 1) + 2 and (0 + 2) + 1 being two spellings of 3, so a
# reading that shares only equal spellings follows every path, about 2 a
# step, while one that folds the accumulators by value keeps k + 1 values
# at step k: a dynamic programme over the reachable sums, which is what
# the definitional program leaves to the implementation. The accumulator is used once on
# every path, as the method body passes it on once, so the set of answers
# is the set of sums and no product of two choices.
#
# THE SNAPSHOT is the set of those sums, each the canonical binary
# numeral. PROOF that S(P) is the snapshot: every read of a hierarchy of width W >= 2
# spells W - 1 empty sets [], which no choice removes and only the
# reduction of the read discards, so a term in which an instance is still
# to be unfolded holds []; a yield, which holds no set, is therefore
# reached only along a choice sequence that ends every recursion, and run recurses on the unary numeral n, one level less at
# each call whatever step chooses; each such end is a sum of n
# increments, and its normal form is that sum's canonical numeral.
#
# READINGS (2026-09-29, a probe in a fresh process per reading,
# every answer of lambda_jit_scott_decoding:decoded/4 collected, 10 s,
# 256 MB, 256 MB, the increments {1, 2}): weak_head reads n = 2, 4, 6 and
# 8 in 25, 123, 809 and 5313 ms and is stopped from 10; tabling(weak_head)
# reads them in 16, 54, 225 and 1107 ms and n = 10 in 4648 ms, and is
# stopped from 12: about 2.1 a step, the growth of the paths.
# LIMITS: the family's, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB.

#   problem(?Point, ?Count, ?Increments)
#
# Each text is from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes,
# imported from corpora/library/text/cbor. Each number is from_cbor of an
# integer literal, a Scott integer, imported from corpora/library/integer/cbor.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
